// TEST: a function writes a module-level plain let
// ERROR: BL4005 @ 10:30
// ERROR-CONTAINS: a captured binding may be written only when it was declared `let mut`
// D9 (deep review, the user's ruling of 2026-11-14; formalism 2.7): a plain
// `let` is writable in the callable that defines it, nested blocks included.
// A callable that only CAPTURES it -- a nested function, a lambda, a kernel, a
// top-level function over a module binding -- writes it only when it was
// declared `let mut`. This used to compile and print x = 2.
// (mutability/018 is the accepted `let mut` twin.)
let x = 1
function bump() -> Int32 = { x = x + 1; x }
let r = bump()
